/-
# RG-Schur mass-generation witness: blocking a null chain generates
# non-null effective terms

DRAFT (kernel-clean; no `s o r r y`). The registered "dynamics" witness of
the two-day carrier run (2026-07-07): per-edge null nilpotency is NOT
stable under one decimation (Schur-complement) step, and the obstruction
coefficient is exactly the pairwise null-direction pairing.

## The statement family

* `null_pair_prod_sq_eq_pairing_smul` (abstract, any associative algebra):
  if `a * a = 0`, `b * b = 0`, and `a * b + b * a = k • 1`, then
  `(a * b) * (a * b) = k • (a * b)`. So the product of two null Clifford
  edge terms fails to be nilpotent exactly when their pairing `k` is
  nonzero - and for null covectors, nonzero pairing means non-collinear.
* Concrete light-cone pair `nullL = !![0,1;0,0]`, `nullN = !![0,0;1,0]`
  (each square-zero, anticommutator `1`): the effective edge term
  `nullL * nullN` is a nonzero idempotent, hence NOT nilpotent
  (`nullL_mul_nullN_not_nilpotent`).
* Schur wiring (`chain_schurComplement_eq`): on the 3-site chain
  `v1 - h - v2` with hidden middle block `1` and null couplings, the
  Schur complement (the `schurComplement` of
  `PhysicsSM.NullStrand.DualSolder.SpectralSchur`) equals
  `-(fromBlocks 0 (nullL*nullN) (nullN*nullL) 0)`: decimation induces a
  direct `v1 - v2` edge whose block is non-nilpotent
  (`effective_edge_not_nilpotent`), although no such edge existed before
  blocking and every original edge term was null.
* Negative control (`collinear_schurComplement_eq_zero`): if the two
  couplings are COLLINEAR (`t • nullL` against `nullL`, any `t`), the
  entire effective coupling vanishes - nullity survives blocking exactly
  on collinear (massless) configurations. This is what makes the witness
  a statement about mass, not an artifact.
* Bonus (`effective_total_sq_eq_zero`): the TOTAL effective operator is
  still square-zero on this chain; the failure of nullity is precisely a
  per-edge statement, which is why the program's per-edge nilpotency
  convention is the right level for the RG question.

## Reading and claim boundary

Kinematically (trusted layer) mass is pairwise null disagreement
(`det P = sum |psi_i wedge psi_j|^2`). This file shows the dynamical
counterpart at finite level: one decimation step converts the SAME
pairwise pairing into a non-null effective edge coefficient. It is ONE
finite Schur step - no RG flow, no fixed points, no continuum claim.
"Mass-like" is used only in the docstrings, never in a statement.

## Provenance

The Schur-complement effective-operator identity is classical (Loewdin
